    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 7,
     "s": "ON THE MORNING OF CHRIST’S NATIVITY",
     "level": 3
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 7,
     "s": "(1629)",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 7,
     "s": "I",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 7,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "THIS is the month, and this the happy morn,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Wherein the Son of Heaven’s eternal King,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of wedded maid and Virgin Mother born,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Our great redemption from above did bring;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For so the holy sages once did sing,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That he our deadly forfeit should release,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And with his Father work us a perpetual peace.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 7,
     "s": "II",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 7,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "That glorious Form, that Light unsufferable,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And that far-beaming blaze of majesty,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Wherewith he wont at Heaven’s high council-table",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To sit the midst of Trinal Unity,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "He laid aside, and, here with us to be,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Forsook the Courts of everlasting Day,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And chose with us a darksome house of mortal clay.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 7,
     "s": "III",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 7,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Say, Heavenly Muse, shall not thy sacred vein",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Afford a present to the Infant God?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Hast thou no verse, no hymn, or solemn strain,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To welcome him to this his new abode,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Now while the heaven, by the Sun’s team untrod,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Hath took no print of the approaching light,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And all the spangled host keep watch in squadrons bright?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 8,
     "s": "IV",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 8,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "See how from far upon the Eastern road",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The star-led Wisards haste with odours sweet!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Oh! run; prevent them with thy humble ode,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And lay it lowly at his blessèd feet;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Have thou the honour first thy Lord to greet,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And join thy voice unto the Angel Quire,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "From out his secret altar touched with hallowed fire.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 8,
     "s": "THE HYMN",
     "level": 3
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 8,
     "s": "I",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 8,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "It was the winter wild,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "While the heaven-born child",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "All meanly wrapt in the rude manger lies;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Nature, in awe to him,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Had doffed her gaudy trim,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "With her great Master so to sympathize:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "It was no season then for her",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To wanton with the Sun, her lusty Paramour.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 8,
     "s": "II",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 8,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Only with speeches fair",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "She woos the gentle air",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "To hide her guilty front with innocent snow,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And on her naked shame,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Pollute with sinful blame,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The saintly veil of maiden white to throw;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Confounded, that her Maker’s eyes",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Should look so near upon her foul deformities.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 8,
     "s": "III",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 8,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "But he, her fears to cease,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Sent down the meek-eyed Peace:",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "She, crowned with olive green, came softly sliding",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Down through the turning sphere,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "His ready Harbinger,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "With turtle wing the amorous clouds dividing;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And, waving wide her myrtle wand,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "She strikes a universal peace through sea and land.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 9,
     "s": "IV",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 9,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "No war, or battail’s sound,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Was heard the world around;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The idle spear and shield were high uphung;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The hookèd chariot stood,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Unstained with hostile blood;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The trumpet spake not to the armèd throng;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And Kings sat still with awful eye,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "As if they surely knew their sovran Lord was by.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 9,
     "s": "V",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 9,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "But peaceful was the night",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Wherein the Prince of Light",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "His reign of peace upon the earth began.",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The winds, with wonder whist,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Smoothly the waters kissed,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Whispering new joys to the mild Ocean,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Who now hath quite forgot to rave,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "While birds of calm sit brooding on the charmèd wave.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 9,
     "s": "VI",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 9,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The stars, with deep amaze,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Stand fixed in steadfast gaze,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Bending one way their precious influence,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And will not take their flight,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "For all the morning light,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Or Lucifer that often warned them thence;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "But in their glimmering orbs did glow,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Until their Lord himself bespake, and bid them go.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 9,
     "s": "VII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 9,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And, though the shady gloom",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Had given day her room,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The Sun himself withheld his wonted speed,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And hid his head for shame,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "As his inferior flame",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The new-enlightened world no more should need:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "He saw a greater Sun appear",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Than his bright Throne or burning axletree could bear.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 10,
     "s": "VIII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 10,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The Shepherds on the lawn,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Or ere the point of dawn,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Sat simply chatting in a rustic row;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Full little thought they than",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "That the mighty Pan",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Was kindly come to live with them below:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Perhaps their loves, or else their sheep,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Was all that did their silly thoughts so busy keep.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 10,
     "s": "IX",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 10,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "When such music sweet",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Their hearts and ears did greet",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "As never was by mortal finger strook,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Divinely-warbled voice",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Answering the stringèd noise,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "As all their souls in blissful rapture took:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The air, such pleasure loth to lose,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With thousand echoes still prolongs each heavenly close.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 10,
     "s": "X",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 10,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Nature, that heard such sound",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Beneath the hollow round",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Of Cynthia’s seat the airy Region thrilling,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Now was almost won",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "To think her part was done,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And that her reign had here its last fulfilling:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "She knew such harmony alone",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Could hold all Heaven and Earth in happier union.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 10,
     "s": "XI",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 10,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "At last surrounds their sight",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "A globe of circular light,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "That with long beams the shamefaced Night arrayed;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The helmèd Cherubim",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And sworded Seraphim",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Are seen in glittering ranks with wings displayed,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Harping in loud and solemn quire,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With unexpressive notes, to Heaven’s newborn Heir.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 11,
     "s": "XII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 11,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Such music (as ’tis said)",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Before was never made,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "But when of old the Sons of Morning sung,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "While the Creator great",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "His constellations set,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And the well-balanced World on hinges hung,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And cast the dark foundations deep,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And bid the weltering waves their oozy channel keep.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 11,
     "s": "XIII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 11,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Ring out, ye crystal spheres!",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Once bless our human ears,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "If ye have power to touch our senses so;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And let your silver chime",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Move in melodious time;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And let the bass of heaven’s deep organ blow;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And with your ninefold harmony",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Make up full consort to the angelic symphony.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 11,
     "s": "XIV",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 11,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "For, if such holy song",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Enwrap our fancy long,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Time will run back and fetch the Age of Gold;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And speckled Vanity",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Will sicken soon and die,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And leprous Sin will melt from earthly mould;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And Hell itself will pass away,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And leave her dolorous mansions to the peering day.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 11,
     "s": "XV",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 11,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Yes, Truth and Justice then",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Will down return to men,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The enamelled arras of the rainbow wearing;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And Mercy set between,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Throned in celestial sheen,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "With radiant feet the tissued clouds down steering;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And Heaven, as at some festival,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Will open wide the gates of her high palace-hall.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 12,
     "s": "XVI",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 12,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "But wisest Fate says No,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "This must not yet be so;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The Babe lies yet in smiling infancy",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "That on the bitter cross",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Must redeem our loss,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "So both himself and us to glorify:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Yet first, to those ychained in sleep,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The wakeful trump of doom must thunder through the deep,",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 12,
     "s": "XVII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 12,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "With such a horrid clang",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "As on Mount Sinai rang,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "While the red fire and smouldering clouds outbrake:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The aged Earth, aghast",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "With terror of that blast,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Shall from the surface to the centre shake,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "When, at the world’s last sessiön,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The dreadful Judge in middle air shall spread his throne.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 12,
     "s": "XVIII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 12,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And then at last our bliss",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Full and perfect is,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "But now begins; for from this happy day",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The Old Dragon under ground,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "In straiter limits bound,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Not half so far casts his usurpèd sway,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And, wroth to see his Kingdom fail,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Swindges the scaly horror of his folded tail.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 12,
     "s": "XIX",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 12,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The Oracles are dumb;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "No voice or hideous hum",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Runs through the archèd roof in words deceiving.",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Apollo from his shrine",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Can no more divine,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "With hollow shriek the steep of Delphos leaving.",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "No nightly trance, or breathèd spell,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Inspires the pale-eyed Priest from the prophetic cell.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 13,
     "s": "XX",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 13,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The lonely mountains o’er,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And the resounding shore,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "A voice of weeping heard and loud lament;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "From haunted spring, and dale",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Edgèd with poplar pale,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The parting Genius is with sighing sent;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "With flower-inwoven tresses torn",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The Nymphs in twilight shade of tangled thickets mourn.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 13,
     "s": "XXI",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 13,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "In consecrated earth,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "And on the holy hearth,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The Lars and Lemures moan with midnight plaint;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "In urns, and altars round,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "A drear and dying sound",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Affrights the Flamens at their service quaint;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And the chill marble seems to sweat,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "While each peculiar power forgoes his wonted seat.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 13,
     "s": "XXII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 13,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Peor and Baälim",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Forsake their temples dim,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "With that twice-battered god of Palestine;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And moonèd Ashtaroth,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Heaven’s Queen and Mother both,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Now sits not girt with tapers’ holy shine:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The Libyc Hammon shrinks his horn;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "In vain the Tyrian maids their wounded Thammuz mourn.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 13,
     "s": "XXIII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 13,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And sullen Moloch, fled,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Hath left in shadows dread",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "His burning idol all of blackest hue;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "In vain with cymbals’ ring",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "They call the grisly king,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "In dismal dance about the furnace blue;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The brutish gods of Nile as fast,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Isis, and Orus, and the dog Anubis, haste.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 14,
     "s": "XXIV",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 14,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Nor is Osiris seen",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "In Memphian grove or green,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Trampling the unshowered grass with lowings loud;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Nor can he be at rest",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Within his sacred chest;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Nought but profoundest Hell can be his shroud;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "In vain, with timbreled anthems dark,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The sable-stolèd Sorcerers bear his worshiped ark.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 14,
     "s": "XXV",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 14,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "He feels from Juda’s land",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The dreaded Infant’s hand;",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The rays of Bethlehem blind his dusky eyn;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Nor all the gods beside",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Longer dare abide,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Not Typhon huge ending in snaky twine:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Our Babe, to show his Godhead true,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Can in his swaddling bands control the damnèd crew.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 14,
     "s": "XXVI",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 14,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "So, when the Sun in bed,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Curtained with cloudy red,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Pillows his chin upon an orient wave,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "The flocking shadows pale",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Troop to the infernal jail,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Each fettered ghost slips to his several grave,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And the yellow-skirted Fays",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Fly after the night-steeds, leaving their moon-loved maze.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 15,
     "s": "XXVII",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 15,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "But see! the Virgin blest",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Hath laid her Babe to rest,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Time is our tedious song should here have ending:",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Heaven’s youngest-teemèd star",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Hath fixed her polished car,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Her sleeping Lord with handmaid lamp attending;",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "And all about the courtly stable",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Bright-harnessed Angels sit in order serviceable.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 15,
     "s": "A PARAPHRASE ON PSALM CXIV",
     "level": 3
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 15,
     "s": "(1624)",
     "level": 4
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 15,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "WHEN the blest seed of Terah’s faithful Son",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "After long toil their liberty had won,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And passed from Pharian fields to Canaan Land,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Led by the strength of the Almighty’s hand,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Jehovah’s wonders were in Israel shown,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "His praise and glory was in Israel known.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That saw the troubled sea, and shivering fled,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And sought to hide his froth-becurlèd head",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Low in the earth; Jordan’s clear streams recoil,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "As a faint host that hath received the foil.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The high huge-bellied mountains skip like rams",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Amongst their ewes, the little hills like lambs.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Why fled the ocean? and why skipped the mountains?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Why turnèd Jordan toward his crystal fountains?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Shake, Earth, and at the presence be aghast",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of Him that ever was and aye shall last,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That glassy floods from rugged rocks can crush,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And make soft rills from fiery flint-stones gush.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 15,
     "s": "PSALM CXXXVI",
     "level": 3
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 15,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "LET us with a gladsome mind",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Praise the Lord for he is kind;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his mercies aye endure,",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "Ever faithful, ever sure.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Let us blaze his Name abroad,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For of gods he is the God;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "O let us his praises tell,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That doth the wrathful tyrants quell;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "That with his miracles doth make",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Amazèd Heaven and Earth to shake;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "That by his wisdom did create",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The painted heavens so full of state;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "That did the solid Earth ordain",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To rise above the watery plain;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "That by his all-commanding might,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Did fill the new-made world with light;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And caused the golden-tressèd Sun",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "All the day long his course to run;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The hornèd Moon to shine by night",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Amongst her spangled sisters bright;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "He, with his thunder-clasping hand,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Smote the first-born of Egypt land;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And, in despite of Pharao fell,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "He brought from thence his Israel;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 16,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The ruddy waves he cleft in twain",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of the Erythraean main;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The floods stood still, like walls of glass,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "While the Hebrew bands did pass;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "But full soon they did devour",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The tawny King with all his power;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "His chosen people he did bless",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "In the wasteful Wilderness;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "In bloody battail he brought down",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Kings of prowess and renown;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "He foiled bold Seon and his host,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That ruled the Amorrean coast;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And large-limbed Og he did subdue,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With all his over-hardy crew;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And to his servant Israel",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "He gave their land, therein to dwell;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "He hath, with a piteous eye,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Beheld us in our misery;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And freed us from the slavery",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of the invading enemy;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "All living creatures he doth feed,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And with full hand supplies their need;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 17,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Let us, therefore, warble forth",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "His mighty majesty and worth;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his, &c.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 18,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "That his mansion hath on high,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Above the reach of mortal eye;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For his mercies aye endure,",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "Ever faithful, ever sure.",
       "i": 4
      }
     ]
    }
